{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012nTSYH2A1FToHdJ82o9zKa","type":"tool_result","content":"# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n`Cache-Control` header at all.\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Upload src/ to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront.\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n\nBUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\nDISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\nPROFILE=\"studio\"\n\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\naws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n  --paths \"/*\" --profile \"$PROFILE\" > /dev/null\n\necho \"deployed\"\nsrc/clases.html:2:<html lang=\"es\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Clases</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"></head>\nsrc/clases.html:3:<body><h1>Clases</h1><ul><li>Torno inicial, sábados</li><li>Modelado, martes</li></ul><div id=\"booking\"></div><script src=\"/booking.js\"></script></body></html>\nsrc/index.html:6:<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\nsrc/index.html:11:<div id=\"booking\"></div>\nsrc/index.html:12:<script src=\"/booking.js\"></script>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"860a3f05-2efd-469c-b0c3-ce08a88a8e85","uuid":"ac051339-1e9a-45c7-881f-20172c067c14","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:38:21.411Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n`Cache-Control` header at all.\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Upload src/ to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront.\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n\nBUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\nDISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\nPROFILE=\"studio\"\n\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\naws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n  --paths \"/*\" --profile \"$PROFILE\" > /dev/null\n\necho \"deployed\"\nsrc/clases.html:2:<html lang=\"es\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Clases</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"></head>\nsrc/clases.html:3:<body><h1>Clases</h1><ul><li>Torno inicial, sábados</li><li>Modelado, martes</li></ul><div id=\"booking\"></div><script src=\"/booking.js\"></script></body></html>\nsrc/index.html:6:<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\nsrc/index.html:11:<div id=\"booking\"></div>\nsrc/index.html:12:<script src=\"/booking.js\"></script>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012nTSYH2A1FToHdJ82o9zKa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
