{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgApbPindRUNKqqtSbGpg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `scripts/deploy.sh` so that every file goes up with its content type and its cache header set together. I tested it only against a fake `aws` command; nothing was deployed or sent to AWS, and the change isn't committed. `ANSWER.md` has the full write-up.\n\n**Cache times:**\n- **HTML, JS and CSS:** `public, max-age=300` (5 minutes). After a deploy, returning visitors pick up the new `booking.js` within minutes, not days.\n- **`assets/`:** `public, max-age=86400` (1 day).\n\n**How the script now works:**\n- **One table** lists each kind of file with its content type (`text/html`, `application/javascript`, `text/css`, `image/png`, `image/svg+xml`) and its cache time.\n- **Uploads come from your local `src/` folder,** with both headers set on each one. I didn't use the bucket-to-bucket `--metadata-directive REPLACE` copy from the guide. Your next normal deploy re-uploads every file with the right headers, so the bucket needs no separate fix.\n- **Unknown file types stop the deploy.** If `src/` has a file the table doesn't cover, the script exits before uploading anything. Add a line to the table for it.\n- **Old files are still deleted** from the bucket, without re-uploading anything (which would strip the headers again).\n- **The script reads the headers back** on `index.html`, `booking.js`, `styles.css` and `logo.png`, and fails if either header is wrong. Then it clears the CloudFront cache as before.\n\n**Testing:** with the fake `aws`, all 6 files got the right headers, none was uploaded twice, and the read-back check passed. Adding an uncovered `robots.txt` stopped the script before any upload. I removed the fake afterwards.\n\n**Choices you may want to change:**\n- **Assets are cached for 1 day, not a year,** because their filenames don't change when the file changes. A year-long cache would keep a replaced logo in browsers for a year.\n- **Old copies are already in browsers.** Visitors who downloaded `booking.js` before this change may keep it for a while longer; the 5-minute rule only applies from the first deploy with the new script.\n\nAfter your first real deploy, check with `curl -sI` that the site and `booking.js` return the right `content-type` and `cache-control`, since a 200 alone proves nothing. Then open the site in a private window."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1677,"cache_read_input_tokens":26955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1677},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"860a3f05-2efd-469c-b0c3-ce08a88a8e85","uuid":"d990b03c-e736-4d0e-ba25-9e79a1058ed7","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:39:30.659Z","request_id":"req_011CgApbPLUUFAARy8VTgGdS"}
